+# N29 CPU-prepared controller contract
+
+This source is preparation only. All real budget adoption, source integration, resource admission, CUDA proof and Dev dispatch are root actions, separately reviewed. No executable production plan or authority is delivered by CPU tests. The original N28 source, accepted closure, proofs and all historical costs remain immutable.
+
+## Fixed science and measurements
+
+The sole profile delta from N28 is `diversity_update_mode=population_relative_trust_v1`. The frozen Phase A helper is unchanged. All four initial RBF calls and ten selected-parent calls now compute the FP32 empirical population RMS radius and row beta, cast the scaled operand to native dtype, and compose the original feasible ray. Initial same-forward and parent-before-original-renoise inputs remain distinct. Native raw operand, scaled operand, beta, radius, raw row norms, final box alpha and actual assigned after-minus-before are separate evidence. `trust_limited_rows` means beta<1; `limited_rows` remains final box alpha<1. Neither is an efficacy gate. `population_trust_overhead_seconds` is host wall including helper/assignment/scalar synchronization, not isolated GPU kernel time; it overlaps the inherited feasible-update host observation and must not be added to that observation as disjoint costs.
+
+The actual guided loop remains 21 model batches, 176 candidate evaluations, 11 scoring batches, ten original resample/renoise/rollout rounds and 14 RBF calls. No extra model, scoring, projector or RNG call is introduced. N28/default branches retain literal old behavior. Configuration validation uses an independent attribute proxy because the production `_EDSConfig` is a frozen dataclass; it never edits the original configuration.
+
+The first guided decision records exactly eleven bounded slots, not all fourteen calls: first active initial call plus ten parent calls. FP32 numeric maximum is 12,804 bytes initial + 10×14,340 bytes parent including actual renoise-entry prefix = 156,204 bytes, below 220 KiB total and 20 KiB/slot. Metadata is independently bounded at 16 KiB/slot including the parent entry record. All-call scalar evidence remains fourteen per guided decision. Actual parent provenance binds allocation→assigned selected offspring→original renoise entry. A future synthetic GPU proof verifies the boundary observer's binding, not a live policy renoise invocation; CPU stub call-chain tests and each live worker supply their respective evidence.
+
+The independent auditor repeats literal FP32 reduction/cast and original ray arithmetic without calling the new helper. It compares shapes/dtypes and contiguous byte views, flattening zero-dimensional radius only for byte comparison. Zero tolerance remains. CPU FP32/BF16 tests do not establish CUDA parity. True zero spread and zero operand are legal; nonzero FP32 square/reduction underflow and nonfinite/support violations fail closed with no epsilon/fallback. BF16 casting/assignment can exceed an exact-real radius bound, which is not claimed. Empirical spread is not calibrated uncertainty, and a concentrated but wrong policy may lose necessary exploration.
+
+## Source and history
+
+`qd_ed_n29_bridge` binds six exact bounded public JSON records: accepted N28 terminal review, its 383-file source, plan, source bridge and tensor proof, and the original exposed ten-task Dev plan. It does not recursively replay historical controllers or native payloads. Closed history is trusted through root's existing accepted metadata attestations. Current source/runtime bytes, provider, resource, plan and budget checks remain live.
+
+Exactly three existing files change: `core/rdt_policy_steer.py`, `scripts/qd_ed_final_runner.py`, `scripts/qd_ed_n23_worker.py`. `reverse-source-v1.json` restores each byte to base52; all other old 380 source files must match. New source paths include the complete old manifest, all N29 helpers, scripts, profile, protocols, bridge and tests. New-mode routing precedes N28 (which is a control in this cohort); old cohort predicates exclude N29. Same-worker audit is CUDA for N28/N29 and CPU for C0/Q0; the model still uses the single assigned GPU. Profile-bound native gates also apply to legitimate zero-guided episodes with absent metrics.
+
+## Exact finite lifecycle
+
+Forty untouched primary cells: task-major tasks0..9 × C0/Q0/N28/N29 using original exposed Dev identities. No result inheritance, retry, recovery or resume. All40 valid, N29≥5/10 and ≥same-cohort C0/Q0, substantive QD/ED and original validity gates are required for Dev promotion. N28 paired gains/losses are reported, not an extra threshold. No validation or formal launcher exists here.
+
+Only after a complete task quadruple, candidate successes + unrun candidate tasks <5 closes `REJECT_NUMERIC_DEV_FUTILITY`; 0/4 is not futile, 0/6 is. Both supervisor and per-cell admission reject continuation past the first futile quadruple. Any invalidity closes `INVALID_OR_INTERRUPTED`, retaining all charged and unreturned attempts. Final reconstruction compares status and independently accepted journal prefixes; disagreement never promotes. Missing cost/usage stays explicit, not zero-imputed. Unknown token calls are derived from each terminal's observed counters.
+
+The prospective root-only finite budget is 578 attempts / 100 GPU hours; bucket caps baseline76, development262, validation180, formal40, recovery20; protected hour reservations validation32/formal12. Local 13.5 GPU hours includes the one tensor proof. This does not guarantee forty worst-case episodes fit. Full remaining primary slot capacity is required, and every dispatch must reserve an entire 1800+40 seconds locally and globally after protected reserves. N29 checks the generic runner's integer-floor/grace arithmetic before generic timeout truncation or reservation. Inability to reserve the full interval raises `ResourceBudgetIncomplete`, launches nothing and closes `RESOURCE_BUDGET_INCOMPLETE`, never scientific rejection. The original user did not separately approve 578; any later finite root adoption must record the existing autonomous delegation faithfully.
+
+The tensor proof is one resource process, 24 cases (6×2 dtypes×2 layouts), 80 seconds active +40 cleanup, zero episodes/model/API/simulator calls. Its full process wall is charged to the existing private health ledger's recovery-hour bucket and cumulative100h. It consumes zero episode-attempt slots. Even reserved/failed proof consumes the single opportunity; no automatic repeat. Exactly one live worker maximum.
+
+## External schemas and root activation order
+
+Disabled templates under the variant root wrap exact expected JSON in `document`, with `executable=false` and unresolved fields. They are not authority files. `source` is the full `{commit, files:[{path,sha256}], sha256}` record; every reference is `{path,sha256}`. Do not hash later proof/review bytes into source: external bindings avoid a circular source freeze.
+
+1. Independently inspect source, preserved failures, 3-file reversal, pure-helper immutability and six accepted history refs; integrate only the final source commit. Rehash current source/runtime and verify current managed Codex/chatgpt login and frozen no-Poe/no-fallback provider. Build `source-equivalence-bridge-v1.json` by `bridge.build(source,c.runtime_ref(),W)` using actual owning imports. No numerical old proof rerun.
+2. Root independently adopts the exact finite amendment in private state under existing locks, setting `n29_budget_authority` to `budget-adoption-v1/authority.json`. Budget authority exact keys and values are in `budget_authority()`: schema, caps, protocol, predecessor, limits, local_gpu_hours, amendment, recorded_at, authority_interpretation, validation_authorized=false, formal_authorized=false. State amendment equals the bound authority amendment.
+3. Write `arithmetic-preflight-source-review-v1.json`; root-created `arithmetic-preflight-adoption-v1/authority.json` binds full source/runtime/review/budget/limits/current boot and explicitly forbids retries and Dev/protected execution. Set only `n29_arithmetic_authority` in state. Write `arithmetic-preflight-release-v1.json`. Root CLI: `PY scripts/qd_ed_n29_backend.py --run`. Its locked admission rechecks GPU7 UUID/EGL/runtime, source, costs, reservations and absence of prior proof/Dev reservation; it immutably writes the one resource plan and metered proof. No extra probe is called by this CPU preparation.
+4. Only after actual proof acceptance, write `final-source-runtime-review-v1.json`; `adoption-v1/authority.json` binds that proof/source/runtime/bridge/protocol/predecessor and fixed13.5h/caps. Set `n29_dev_authority` in state under locks. These two records are exact schemas defined by `final_review()` and `authority()`.
+5. Root CLI: `PY scripts/qd_ed_n29_prepare.py --freeze --output V/plan.frozen.v1.gpu7.json`. Review actual immutable forty commands (actual original n4 observed profiles, seed/runtime refs), protected-data closure and artifact containment. Write `execution-release-v1.json` containing plan ref, exact ordered forty keys, authority, limits/GPU7 and protected=false.
+6. Root CLI: `PY scripts/qd_ed_n29_supervise.py --plan V/plan.frozen.v1.gpu7.json --release V/execution-release-v1.json --status V/execution/supervisor-status-v1.json`. It creates only its operational execution parent, then locks and forbids an existing status/result/reservation. Episode artifacts stay in the dedicated V/artifacts data-volume target; controller/status/result remain V. `result-v1.json` is immutable; no restart/resume. Root later independently reviews terminal metadata and process cleanup. CPU preparation makes no release or performance claim.
+
+All current and future online Stage remains frozen codex_cli/current managed ChatGPT/gpt-6-astra/low/180s. Existing Poe credentials are neither read nor changed; no alternate provider or fallback is added.
